        "original_id": "11c6d5af-008c-554c-8fa5-ad75f85364e3",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Rebecca Rippy, Rhonda Vincent, Don Dixon, Leon Russell, Lucy Kaplansky, Tony Rice, Jim Lauderdale, Bill Mallonee, Tinsley Ellis, John Cowan, Danielle Howle\n- Organizations: Donna the Buffalo, Vigilantes of Love, Old Crow Medicine Show\n- Places: Bluebird Café, Neighborhood Theater, Nashville, Charlotte\n- Roles: singer, songwriter, multi-instrumentalist, producer\n- Topics: roots country, Americana, bluegrass, live performance\n\nFacts:\n- Rhonda Vincent was born on July 13, 1962, and she is an American bluegrass singer, songwriter, and multi-instrumentalist.\n- Rebecca Rippy was born in 1977, and she is an American singer-songwriter most notably associated with the roots country and Americana genres.\n- Rebecca Rippy has played or shared the stage with Don Dixon, Leon Russell, Lucy Kaplansky, Tony Rice, Donna the Buffalo, Jim Lauderdale, Bill Mallonee and the Vigilantes of Love, Tinsley Ellis, John Cowan, Rhonda Vincent, Danielle Howle, and Old Crow Medicine Show.\n- Rebecca Rippy has become a regular performer at the Bluebird Café in Nashville, Tennessee, and at the Neighborhood Theater in Charlotte, North Carolina.",
